{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Anj7eT2Bsu2XubReAqfGZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tpackage com.unityinflow.sample.shipment\n2\t\n3\t/**\n4\t * A shipment raised against an order.\n5\t *\n6\t * This is the baseline (pre-benchmark) shape. BE-003 asks an agent to add a confirm\n7\t * transition; the baseline deliberately has no way to move a shipment out of [CREATED].\n8\t */\n9\tdata class Shipment(\n10\t    val shipmentId: String,\n11\t    val orderId: String,\n12\t    val carrier: String,\n13\t    val status: ShipmentStatus,\n14\t    val quantity: Int = 1,\n15\t)\n16\t\n17\t/**\n18\t * The lifecycle of a shipment.\n19\t *\n20\t * [CANCELLED] is terminal. It is reachable in the fixture only by writing it directly to\n21\t * the repository — there is no cancel endpoint — which is enough for a test to set up the\n22\t * state without giving the benchmark a second unrelated feature to implement.\n23\t */\n24\tenum class ShipmentStatus {\n25\t    CREATED,\n26\t    CONFIRMED,\n27\t    DELIVERED,\n28\t    CANCELLED,\n29\t}\n30\t\n31\tdata class CreateShipmentRequest(\n32\t    val shipmentId: String,\n33\t    val orderId: String,\n34\t    val carrier: String,\n35\t    val quantity: Int? = null,\n36\t)\n37\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WEWcshuj5h41Y6RdWesoV3","session_id":"db6ff8fc-02cf-48f4-a54d-512a55c9ddf2","uuid":"db0d79bb-b645-44a0-a9f5-82e85e353ab5","timestamp":"2026-09-25T09:49:33.586Z","subagent_type":"implementer","task_description":"Implementer completion"}
